---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    My work has mostly revolved around one broad question: how do we turn
    messy information and complicated processes into systems that are
    actually useful?
  </p>

  <p>
    That has taken me through data engineering, machine learning,
    operations research, knowledge graphs, backend development and,
    more recently, LLM and agentic AI systems.
  </p>

  <p>
    I've worked on projects across pharma, retail, finance, venture
    capital and optimization-heavy environments. Depending on the problem,
    my work has ranged from building ETL pipelines and data models to
    designing RAG systems, optimizing distributed processing and building
    backend services.
  </p>

  <p>
    Teaching has become an important part of my professional life.
    I've conducted hundreds of technical interviews, mentored engineers,
    organized workshops and given talks on topics ranging from Python and
    databases to GraphRAG, AI systems and software engineering.
  </p>

  <p>
    I enjoy situations where technology meets something less technical:
    how people make decisions, how teams work, how we learn, and how
    tools change our way of thinking.
  </p>

  <p>
    This website is where I collect things I've built, ideas I'm exploring,
    articles, and whatever else I find worth remembering or sharing.
  </p>

  <style>
    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    p {
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
